    {
      "text": "wash your feet, Gen. 18:4 (19:2; 24:32; 43:24). Aaron and his sons thou … shalt wash, Ex. 29:4 (40:12). it shall be washed the second time, Lev. 13:58. priest shall wash his clothes, Num. 19:7. elders … shall wash their hands over the heifer, Deut. 21:6. from the roof he saw a woman washing herself, 2 Sam. 11:2. wash in Jordan seven times, 2 Kgs. 5:10. ten lavers … to wash in them, 2 Chr. 4:6. will wash mine hands in innocency, Ps. 26:6 (73:13). Wash me throughly from mine iniquity, Ps. 51:2. wash me, and I shall be whiter than snow, Ps. 51:7. righteous … shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked, Ps. 58:10. generation … is not washed from their filthiness, Prov. 30:12. Wash you, make you clean, Isa. 1:16. Lord shall have washed away the filth of the daughters of Zion, Isa. 4:4 (2 Ne. 14:4). though thou wash thee with nitre, Jer. 2:22. Jerusalem, wash thine heart from wickedness, Jer. 4:14.",
