    {
      "text": "when thou fastest … wash thy face, Matt. 6:17 (3 Ne. 13:17). they wash not their hands when they eat, Matt. 15:2. Pilate … washed his hands before the multitude, Matt. 27:24. except they wash their hands oft, eat not, Mark 7:3. eat bread with unwashen hands, Mark 7:5. began to wash his feet with tears, Luke 7:38. Pharisee … marvelled that he had not first washed before dinner, Luke 11:38. Go, wash in the pool of Siloam, John 9:7. began to wash the disciples’ feet, John 13:5. ye also ought to wash one another’s feet, John 13:14. be baptized, and wash away thy sins, Acts 22:16 (Alma 7:14; D&C 39:10). ye are washed … sanctified, 1 Cor. 6:11. cleanse it with the washing of water by the word, Eph. 5:26. if she have washed the saints’ feet, 1 Tim. 5:10. he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, Titus 3:5. stood only in … divers washings, Heb. 9:10. having … our bodies washed with pure water, Heb. 10:22. sow that was washed to her wallowing, 2 Pet. 2:22. him that … washed us from our sins in his own blood, Rev. 1:5. they … have washed their robes, Rev. 7:14.",
